WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Google just dropped a new ai model that can juggle a million words of context at once. A real school project or a messy work task can now sit in one helper from start to finish. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, episode 232. How that memory works under the hood comes next. Then a 3D world builder you can try, and quick bits. Google on its blog released Gemini 4 Neon today. A model aimed at hard programming jobs, research heavy work, and science processes that take many steps

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.080
Google says it finishes those jobs quickly all the way through, not just the first

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.780
question. Access starts immediately for paying Google AI Pro and Ultra users in the Gemini

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.760
app. Those same paid plans can use it inside anti-gravity, and it is in Gemini for business

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:53.300
too. Paying users can also pick it in Google AI Studio through the paid Gemini API, a doorway

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.360
for plugging the model into other tools.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.740
Neon reads text, images, video, audio, and PDFs.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.380
Those document files you download for class.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.100
All together, it turns that mix into finished things with a real shape, like a report or

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:08.780
a code fix.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.960
You get four thinking levels you can adjust, swapping a faster answer for a more careful

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:14.920
one while you work.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.560
On a public score board called the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, Neon scores

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.540
is 61 at its X-high thinking level. That rank is third overall and it sits ahead of comparable

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.320
models. It reaches second place on the Val's index. It also lands on the Pareto Frontier,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.080
meaning it is in the group with the strongest trade-offs, not a single isolated win. Inside

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.520
the new Agent Arena index, it ranks second on Steerability, meaning it adapts cleanly when

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.880
you correct it mid-task. In Google's own anti-gravity tests, Neon posted the lowest

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.540
fabrication rate they have seen so far, meaning it invented the fewest fake details.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.380
It also shines at following instructions that come in many steps.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:04.480
For company and analysis work, it combines spreadsheets, PDFs, charts, audio, and video in one pass.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.300
It takes first place on both the legal research bench and the tax agent bench.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.000
Tests of legal research and tax tasks.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.980
It leads most categories on surge AI tests covering finance,

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.040
sense, accounting, spreadsheet modeling, and following complex rules.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:26.080
It scores 73.5% on chartography, a test of reading dense professional charts.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.220
It reaches 75.8% on Agents last exam version 1.1.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.860
It takes first place overall on Zapier's Automation Bench with 56.3%.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:44.000
On And On Labs Vending Bench 2, a long-running pretend business, it scores $16,843.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.500
dollars. The price is $3 per million input tokens, $0.15 per million cashed input tokens,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.640
and $15 per million output tokens. Tokens are tiny chunks the model splits text into.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.220
Input is what you send, output is what it writes, and cashed means reused at a lower price.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.380
If you already use AI for homework, art, or learning a skill, this is meant to hold a

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.940
whole project, not just a single chat. You can try Gemini 4 Neon right now with a paid

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:19.280
Google AI Pro or Ultra subscription. Open the Gemini app or Google AI Studio and select it from

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.960
the model drop down. Type a request such as read this PDF and turn the key points into a study

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:31.195
guide with quiz questions at the end and watch how it treats a longer pile of material. A context

00:03:31.195 --> 00:03:36.735
window is the working memory a model like Neon uses while you work with it. Your phone chat usually

00:03:36.735 --> 00:03:41.535
keeps just the latest bubbles on screen, so this morning's plan has already scrolled away.

00:03:41.535 --> 00:03:47.115
First, you send a question. Maybe with files and notes attached. Second, Neon does not

00:03:47.115 --> 00:03:51.595
only stare at the newest sentence. Third, it can scan back through everything already

00:03:51.595 --> 00:03:56.555
in that window so the answer stays consistent with the whole pile. Fourth, you do not have

00:03:56.555 --> 00:04:01.475
to repeat yourself or chop the project into tiny pieces that fit a smaller memory. The

00:04:01.475 --> 00:04:05.695
chat bubbles that vanished on your phone are still sitting in Neon's window, which holds

00:04:05.695 --> 00:04:11.115
1 million tokens, roughly the length of a full novel. Once you picture that window as working

00:04:11.115 --> 00:04:16.684
memory, the giant context claims sound like a bigger desk, not a magic trick. Project

00:04:16.684 --> 00:04:22.704
Genie just opened as a full creative ecosystem, and Google said so in a post on X. You describe

00:04:22.704 --> 00:04:27.404
a world in plain words, and AI agent is a helper that acts rather than only chatting.

00:04:27.964 --> 00:04:32.744
It builds a three-dimensional space with depth, like a game level you walk around and edit

00:04:32.744 --> 00:04:38.084
while you watch. The update brings Genie 4, which Google calls the most realistic interactive

00:04:38.084 --> 00:04:43.424
of world model yet. It now has real-time editing and native audio, so the world makes its

00:04:43.424 --> 00:04:48.304
own sound. You can type to change the weather, drop in new characters, or redirect the

00:04:48.304 --> 00:04:53.924
action as it happens. A new Project Genie agent creates worlds through ordinary conversation.

00:04:54.644 --> 00:04:59.584
Gemini offers suggestions that fit the scene you already made. The release includes a community

00:04:59.584 --> 00:05:05.924
gallery where people explore, publish, and remix worlds. Debut collaborations include Villa Jala

00:05:05.924 --> 00:05:12.304
with Will, also known as BLVCKL, G-H-T, and the Life of Ants with Anand Gandhi.

00:05:13.024 --> 00:05:17.824
Genie 3 upgrades are in the mix too, with sessions extended to 3 minutes and the ability

00:05:17.824 --> 00:05:19.124
to chain worlds together.

00:05:19.824 --> 00:05:25.844
It also adds 360-degree panorama image grounding, which lets a full-surround photo anchor the

00:05:25.844 --> 00:05:26.104
scene.

00:05:26.824 --> 00:05:32.284
Eligible Google AI ultra-subscribers can use it now, and a wait list is open for pro-users.

00:05:32.284 --> 00:05:37.984
Go to the Gemini app or Google AI Studio, look for the Project Genie section, and type this.

00:05:38.484 --> 00:05:42.464
A cozy rainy cafe at night with jazz playing and a cat on the window sill.

00:05:43.084 --> 00:05:46.704
See what world it builds, then try changing the weather with another sentence.

